/-!
# Flatness at a point of a relative quasi-regular immersion

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes and `i : Z ⟶ X` a relative quasi-regular immersion
over `S`.  At a point of the image of `i` whose local ring on `X` is Noetherian, `f` is flat.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.flat_of_regular_quotient_flat`: if `h` is a nonzerodivisor in the maximal
  ideal of a Noetherian local `A`-algebra `B` and `B ⧸ (h)` is flat over `A`, then `B` is flat
  over `A`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.flat_of_regularSequence_quotient_flat`: the same for the quotient by a
  regular sequence inside the maximal ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.flat_of_comp_surjective_of_regular_ker`: if `g : B →+* C` is surjective with
  kernel generated by such a regular sequence and `g ∘ f` is flat, then `f` is flat.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_regularSequence_ker_stalkMap`: at a point with Noetherian local ring,
  the kernel of the stalk map of a quasi-regular immersion is generated by a regular sequence in
  the maximal ideal.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatAt_of_isRelativeQuasiRegularImmersion`: a morphism `f : X ⟶ S` is flat
  at every point of the image of a relative quasi-regular immersion over `S` whose local ring is
  Noetherian.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 063T](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063T)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 063G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063G)
-/

@[expose] public section

